[{"body":"The campaign currently proposes competing owners for the Asahi EBIOS tablet family. Reconcile their source scopes before integration; the evidence below does not establish identical historical excipients or authorize a maintained-owner merge.\n\n- Worker01 `KG26-PROP-172-IDENTITY` promotes existing `data/ingredients/unmapped/EBIOS.yaml` from `UNMAPPED_0380` to `kgmicrobe.ingredient:ebios`. Its payload SHA256 is `ad84636fcfdfa606ce97d7655145ed968b3c0d36e2387b5ccad1850245ffe91b`.\n- Worker02 `a2-proposal-nbrc1132-asahi-ebios-tablets` proposes a new `kgmicrobe.ingredient:nbrc1132_asahi_ebios_tablets` owner. Its payload SHA256 is `3275012aad49e7d7e353507d106a3a26c8b2313fad80e5e587ade3bec857bc3c`. Its rationale treats the existing EBIOS owner as an unresolved EBIOS/P2G record.\n- The existing owner's before hash is `130f1d9a20d6e16b9a10939a7251242d290bc8b13eb2a140be697e7b86cf87a4`. Its creation history identifies MediaDive ingredient1953. That exact frozen source record explicitly says dried yeast tablets, 10g. P2G occurs in inherited research prose and does not replace this source continuity.\n\n[JCM969](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=969) identifies EBIOS dried yeast tablets, 10g, with an Asahi Food & Healthcare footnote. Worker06 case92/TOGOM1019 is this same source context. The frozen NBRC1132 context in worker02 identifies Asahi Breweries tablets distributed by Tanabe. These facts require a reviewed product-family/source boundary decision; different recipe identifiers alone do not establish distinct product identities, and different historical supplier wording does not prove equal formulations.\n\nThe worker06 bounded finding receipt is `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-06/successor-v3/research-b/ebios-cross-shard-finding.json`, SHA256 `0fa69e99e546e64f0f7577efd9bef50114db34a7c705231c513479079311e9fd`. It preserves both exact proposal objects and payloads, all three frozen source cases, original owner history and JCM969 capture provenance. The original JCM969 capture SHA256 is `e0a5b7970d48f4ec47c071f9f21eb039465e95b58ca05efb3a4ed9a69508a1ca`, retrieved `2026-11-08T05:07:06.324562+00:00`.\n\nRequired outcome: check the established owner first; reconcile the uninstalled proposals with all author lineages and exact source links retained. Keep tablet form separate from P2G/yeast extract, preserve unknown historical excipients and doses, and avoid a global bare-brand alias. Worker06 can independently propose its exact JCM969/tablet scope against the existing owner, with this cross-shard dependency explicit. The coordinator must independently review the eventual combined payload and source applicability before application or release.\n\nThis was found during issue1217's authorized bounded EBIOS work and is filed before the worker06 EBIOS correction. An all-state read of 679 issue titles/bodies found EBIOS only in issue1217, which does not resolve this cross-worker owner conflict. No other worker was edited; no maintained change or merge has occurred.\n","number":1221,"state":"open","title":"Reconcile competing Asahi EBIOS tablet proposal owners before campaign integration","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1221"},{"body":"Final coordinator review of two published source-review shards found that several no-change outcomes defer already-authorized curation rather than identify a missing scientific fact. Worker04 head `0d2c73e5aee5adb88782537755472d9ca0c5c3cd`; worker08 head `7efd3f8b98f9e822431dcb510c2c242a2569cfc7`; both depend on #1158 at `e000d66`.\n\nConcrete examples:\n\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:b9a945a3356d0c885eea986a2f6223e78c8e7d7163ee95629061a640294cbbe8` (H2O deionized) correctly distinguishes deionization from distillation, but its remaining requirement is to perform native owner lookup and use or create the appropriately scoped owner. [DSMZ533](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium533.pdf) explicitly identifies deionized water in both main and trace stock. No proposal or completed lookup disposition accompanies that deferred step.\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:e69128522cfe555f63dd51d4a23ece86363290b3839180386b090f368b28d1cc` (glycine-NaOH buffer) preserves a source-defined concentration and pH, and correctly finds a receiving-medium volume transcription error. [JCM906](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=906) specifies the separately prepared buffer. The decision defers representing the stock without explaining which missing fact prevents a bounded preparation identity. It must not be equated to pure glycine or assigned invented titrant amounts.\n- Worker04 case `CM_NAME:2f91fab8feab468a33e48d01e2f0a1363b9ad70816766c69a1e8d68c0ed6f8d5` describes the [NBRC15](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=15) treated, clarified V-8 preparation but defers representing it until later curation. Lack of a molecular mapping or extraction yield does not by itself establish that a source-qualified preparation cannot be represented with an honest partial assertion.\n\nRelated outcomes defer normality-qualified NaOH stocks, source-specific top layers, C9322 supplied-form review, and malted wheat meal because an exact molecular/ontology mapping or later complete-owner review is absent. These are leads for reassessment, not predetermined identity approvals. Genuine solvent, formulation, provenance or supplied-form uncertainties may remain after primary research.\n\nReassess the full no-change cohorts against MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections3/6 and add-media. Complete supported proposal work, or state the precise scientific fact still missing and the actual primary-source searches. Keep receiving-medium dose/unit repair separate from ingredient identity. Never invent concentrations, solvent, chemistry, product equivalence, component completeness, or exact ontology matches; preserve all native holds and old review bytes. Require separate skeptical review of successor evidence/payloads and ordinary commits/pushes on the existing worker branches. No maintained data or export approval is requested from workers.\n\nThis extends the same class of completeness problem seen in #1163 and #1193 to distinct final shards; those earlier findings remain preserved. Exact frozen decisions and capture hashes are retained in the coordinator's immutable `w04-w08-deferred-curation-v1/review-inputs.json` and will accompany the campaign evidence. This is a review-completeness finding, not a statement that every listed source must map.\n","number":1201,"state":"open","title":"Complete deferred source-qualified curation in final unmatched review shards","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201"}]
